{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassEndomorphism.TopologicalMassConjecture","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassEndomorphism.TopologicalMassConjecture","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TopologicalMass.flatVortex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TopologicalMass.flatVortex","kind":"def","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/topological-mass-conjecture.lean#L172-L197","doc":"**Flat-vortex satisfiability witness** (a `def`, deliberately NOT an\n`instance`).  The data `holonomy = 0`, `N = 0`, `mass = 0` satisfies\n`decomp` by `simp`.  It shows only that the class is consistent; it\nencodes none of the conjectural content.\n\nThis was a global `instance` until 2026-10-10 (bean `tmvac`).  As an\ninstance over an arbitrary `vortex` it was found by typeclass resolution\nfor every vortex type, so any `[TopologicalDecompositionMass ℝ vortex]`\nbinder was discharged with all-zero data and `M.mass` resolved to `0`.\nThat preempted the §3b-cond hypothesis rather than witnessing it.  Use\nit explicitly, e.g. `@mass_nonneg ℝ _ _ _ v (flatVortex v)`, where a\nconsistency check is wanted.\n\nNote that `mass` is itself a field of the class, so `decomp` relates\nfields of one instance to each other.  It does not tie `mass` to a mass\ndefined independently of the instance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TopologicalMass.mass_mono_of_extra_dilog","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TopologicalMass.mass_mono_of_extra_dilog","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/topological-mass-conjecture.lean#L145-L170","doc":"**Adding a blow-up centre does not decrease mass.**\n\nIf two vortices share the same holonomy and all but one dilogarithm\nvalue, the one with the extra blow-up centre has mass ≥ the other. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TopologicalMass.mass_gt_holonomy_of_dilog_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TopologicalMass.mass_gt_holonomy_of_dilog_pos","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/topological-mass-conjecture.lean#L130-L143","doc":"**Blow-ups strictly increase mass above the holonomy.**\n\nWhen N ≥ 1 and all dilogarithm values are strictly positive,\nthe mass strictly exceeds the holonomy contribution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TopologicalMass.mass_eq_holonomy_of_flat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TopologicalMass.mass_eq_holonomy_of_flat","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/topological-mass-conjecture.lean#L115-L128","doc":"**In the flat case (no blow-ups), mass equals the holonomy.**\n\nWhen N = 0 the brane boundary has no exceptional divisors, so the\ntransient (dilogarithm) piece vanishes and mass = holonomy. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TopologicalMass.mass_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TopologicalMass.mass_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/topological-mass-conjecture.lean#L100-L113","doc":"**Mass is non-negative.**\n\nBoth the holonomy and all dilogarithm values are non-negative, so\ntheir sum is non-negative.  This is the physical content that\nmass ≥ 0 follows purely from the categorical structure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TopologicalMass.mass_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TopologicalMass.mass_unique","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/topological-mass-conjecture.lean#L88-L98","doc":"**Mass is uniquely determined by the decomposition.**\n\nAny element m agreeing with holonomy + Σ dilog equals the class mass.\nIn other words, the decomposition `decomp` has at most one solution\nfor `mass` given the holonomy and dilogarithm data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TopologicalMass.TopologicalDecompositionMass.decomp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TopologicalMass.TopologicalDecompositionMass.decomp","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/topological-mass-conjecture.lean#L82-L82","doc":"**The decomposition equation** (the conjecture). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TopologicalMass.TopologicalDecompositionMass.mass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TopologicalMass.TopologicalDecompositionMass.mass","kind":"def","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/topological-mass-conjecture.lean#L80-L80","doc":"The total categorical mass. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TopologicalMass.TopologicalDecompositionMass.dilog_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TopologicalMass.TopologicalDecompositionMass.dilog_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/topological-mass-conjecture.lean#L78-L78","doc":"Each dilogarithm value is non-negative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TopologicalMass.TopologicalDecompositionMass.dilog","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TopologicalMass.TopologicalDecompositionMass.dilog","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/topological-mass-conjecture.lean#L76-L76","doc":"Quantum-dilogarithm values ‖Φ_q(zᵢ)‖ at each blow-up centre. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TopologicalMass.TopologicalDecompositionMass.N","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TopologicalMass.TopologicalDecompositionMass.N","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/topological-mass-conjecture.lean#L74-L74","doc":"Number of exceptional divisors (blow-up centres). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TopologicalMass.TopologicalDecompositionMass.holonomy_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TopologicalMass.TopologicalDecompositionMass.holonomy_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/topological-mass-conjecture.lean#L72-L72","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TopologicalMass.TopologicalDecompositionMass.holonomy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TopologicalMass.TopologicalDecompositionMass.holonomy","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/topological-mass-conjecture.lean#L71-L71","doc":"Gauge-holonomy contribution ‖Hol_∇(ϱ₀; G)‖. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TopologicalMass.TopologicalDecompositionMass.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TopologicalMass.TopologicalDecompositionMass.mk","kind":"ctor","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/topological-mass-conjecture.lean#L68-L68","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.TopologicalMass.TopologicalDecompositionMass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.TopologicalMass.TopologicalDecompositionMass","kind":"class","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/topological-mass-conjecture.lean#L54-L82","doc":"**Vortex mass decomposition conjecture** (axiomatized as a class).\n\nAn instance `TopologicalDecompositionMass R vortex` asserts that\nthe mass of `vortex` decomposes as\n    mass = holonomy + Σᵢ dilog i,\nwhere:\n- `holonomy` is the gauge-holonomy norm ‖Hol_∇(ϱ₀; G)‖ ≥ 0,\n- `dilog i` is the quantum-dilogarithm norm ‖Φ_q(zᵢ)‖ ≥ 0\n  at the i-th blow-up centre,\n- `N` is the number of exceptional divisors.\n\nThe `decomp` field is the conjecture itself; instances supply it\nas an axiomatic hypothesis.  All theorems below are sorry-free. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:topological-decomposition-mass","label":"prop:topological-decomposition-mass","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/topological-mass-conjecture.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}